  "problem_statement": "feat(memory): cross-project global user memory (~/.wells/memory/)\n\nNew wells.user_memory module: standing preferences that apply to\nevery project, not just the one you're in -- the same category of\nthing Claude Code's own auto-memory keeps across conversations.\nComplements (doesn't replace) AGENTS.md, which stays per-repo and\nfinisher-managed.\n\nEntries are small <name>.md files (front-matter: name/description/\ntype) under ~/.wells/memory/. Unlike skills/personas, bodies are\ninjected directly and in full -- these are meant to be short standing\nfacts, not on-demand procedures -- capped by a total-size budget so an\naccumulated store can't runaway-bloat every prompt. Wired into\nexecutor.py's system prompt unconditionally (even in compact mode,\nalongside principles) since these are exactly the kind of explicit\nreminder a weaker/local model benefits from most.\n\n/memory CLI command (list/show/add/edit/remove) + MemoryScreen/\nMemoryEditScreen TUI modal, mirroring /agents and /skills' existing\nUX. New WELLS_USER_MEMORY /config toggle. No safety-gate on writes --\nthis is a global per-user file outside any workspace, closer to\n/config's un-gated settings writes than a workspace mutation.",
